//! MEMORY — a sealed range of physical memory, and the whole of its v1
//! surface (spec §2.5; sawos design 2 D-2).
//!
//! It sits one step above the floor and names nothing else: a region is
//! authority over bytes, so the type is a handle, a `deinit` that releases it,
//! and no operations at all. What a caller DOES with a region — hand it to
//! `System.process_create`, give it to a child — is written where those ops
//! are, in `sos.system`, which is why this file is imported by that one and
//! not the other way round.

import sosabi.{MemoryHandle, NO_HANDLE}

import sos.floor.{sos_handle_release}

/// A handle to a Memory — a sealed range of physical memory.
///
/// THE FIRST SLICE OF §2.5's OBJECT, and its whole v1 surface is being NAMED:
/// a process receives regions at boot through `Process.boot_handle_next` and
/// passes them to `System.process_create`. There is no `map()`, no `alloc()`,
/// no sub-range and no way to read the bounds — a region is authority over
/// bytes, not a description of them. Unit 4 is where pools, derivation,
/// mapping and memory types arrive; nothing here forecloses any of it.
///
/// Built by `Process.boot_handle_next` and by nothing else — no word
/// constructor, no word extractor, the module docstring's rule.
///
/// **IT IS `NoCopy`, AND DROPPING IT RELEASES THE HANDLE** (sawos design 3 D-5),
/// which SUPERSEDES this docstring's own unit-2 paragraph explaining why it was
/// a plain value. Both reasons that paragraph gave have been answered rather
/// than overridden. The OWNING tier is here, so a move-only handle's drop now
/// does something — it is the enforcement the discipline was waiting for. And
/// the boot-handle record's shape is what changed to fit: see `BootHandle` in
/// `sos.system`, whose `Memory` is an optional the caller TAKES rather than a
/// field it would have had to partially move out of.
public struct Memory {
    public(package) handle: MemoryHandle,
}

extension Memory: NoCopy {
    /// Drop is release; see `System`'s deinit for the sentinel and the discard.
    func deinit(&var self) {
        if self.handle != NO_HANDLE {
            let _ = sos_handle_release(self.handle)
        }
    }
}
